asset:        io.github.dawgon2.Revolution.svg
title:        Revolution app icon, Linux hicolor scalable (512 px PNG inside SVG)
author:       Unknown photographer (Soviet Russia, c. 1918-1920); icon made by Claude (agent) for the Revolution fork
source:       Vladimir Lenin speaking from a rostrum in Moscow, c. 1918-1920; photographer unknown. This copy: from The Salt Lake Tribune, commentary of 2017-11-12 (https://www.sltrib.com/opinion/commentary/2017/11/12/leonid-bershidsky-the-legacy-of-1917-lives-on-outside-russia/), supplied by the fork owner (@dawgon2)
license:      Public domain (published before 1931: public domain in the US; Soviet photograph by an unknown author published before 1943: public domain in Russia)
added:        2026-10-17 by Claude (agent) for @dawgon2 (FORK-PLAN §1a.103)
notes:        Cropped, greyscale, rounded corners (radius 112/512) by tools/fork/revolution-icon.sh from revolution-photo.png. Replaces FilmCraft's owl icon in the fork; filmcraft.svg, filmcraft-small.svg and filmcraft.icns are still upstream's owl (not used by the Linux build).
